      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re optimizing for throughput then we need to keep the waiting here small.  There\u0027s a built in 100ms wait in the Kafka protocol itself that I don\u0027t see a way to modify in the kafka-python library.  This wait is for a situation where the return from Kafka was no data at all so the total wait time would be 110ms plus any scheduling jitter.  That seems more than enough and I saw no adverse effects in my testing.  In other testing Kafka handled requests at a ~30ms interval with no trouble.",
